{
  "_comment": [
    "E14 (code-quality audit 2026-11-05): ONE adversarial table for every copy of the SSRF guard.",
    "Copies (Workers do not import from each other, so each keeps its own code):",
    "  scanner/src/safe-fetch.ts validateTargetUrl + safeFetch      profile public",
    "  mcp-server/src/site-fetch.ts validateTargetUrl + safeFetch   profile public",
    "  scanner/src/prospect-scan.ts assertProspectUrl               profile prospect",
    "  outreach/src/safety.ts safeHttpsUrl + research.ts safeFetch  profile prospect",
    "Each Worker's own test suite runs its copies against this file, so a copy that drifts fails its Worker's tests.",
    "reject: every copy must refuse. accept: every copy must allow.",
    "profiles: rows where the two profiles intentionally differ (prospect is https-only, no punycode, no trailing dot).",
    "Scope of the prospect profile: outreach applies it to every hop it fetches itself; the scanner applies it to the",
    "RPC entry URL only (assertProspectUrl). Hops the scanner then fetches during that scan (redirects, discovered",
    "links) go through the public guard, which still refuses every reject row below (open follow-up, not SSRF).",
    "redirects: every fetching copy follows only follow_statuses, never a no_follow_status, re-validates every hop",
    "against the reject list, and stops after max_redirects hops."
  ],
